      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The authors review the use of axamon in the complex rehabilitation of neurological patients with movement disorders in the pathology of lumbar spine. Axamon (ipidacrine) stimulates neuromuscular transmission and excitement conduction via nerves and smooth muscles due to the blockade of potassium channels of the excited membrane and cholinesterase inhibition. Authors studied the efficacy of complex therapy of dorsopathy of lumbar spine in 90 patients using axamon, movalis, pantogamum in different combination and manual methodics. Patient's status has been measured clinically and with several scales. The results obtained allow to conclude that the combination of axamon and pantogamum exerts the best theraupetic effect without any side symptoms."},
